Project 3

Resources and documentation:
    This one was pretty easy. I just used my previous projects, the CS 4280 course material,
    and some consultation with the professor.
        
AI Usage:
    None for this project.
        
How to compile:
    1. make sure you are in the "Gavin-Dennis-P3/" directory
    2. in the terminal, run the "make" command to compile the programs
    3. Optionally, run the following commands to execute the program with the following
       test cases: (documentation about test cases at the bottom of this page)
        * make test - runs P3 with tests/P3_test (a file that doesn't exist) as an argument
        * make test1 - runs P3 with tests/P3_test1 as argument
        * make test2 - runs P3 with tests/P3_test2 as argument
        * make test3 - runs P3 with tests/P3_test3 as argument
        * make testGavin - runs P3 with tests/P3_testGavin as argument (the most comprehensive test)
    4. the finished executuble 'P3' can be found in the 'build' directory (Gavin-Dennis-P3/build/)

Problems encountered:
    Nothing this time.

Test cases:
    P3_test1.txt - based on example 1 from assignment specifications. Defines and uses a single variable.
    P3_test2.txt - based on example 2 from assignment specifications. Defines one variable and uses it a couple times.
    P3_test3.txt - based on example 3 from assignment specifications. Defines one variable and attempts to use an undefined variable. Throws an error.
	P3_testGavin - my personal test case from P2. Defines two variables and uses one of them. Has some comments which get filtered out in main.